<Base title="Learn the Research Process"><section class="page-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">INVESTIGATE / LEARN</p><h1>What does research actually look like?</h1><p class="lead">Start with a question. Gather evidence. Examine alternatives. Document what you know—and what you don't.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="container narrow"><ol class="steps"><li>Define a question that evidence could help answer.</li><li>Collect observations and preserve source links.</li><li>Evaluate records, uncertainty, and possible biases.</li><li>Analyze patterns without confusing correlation with causation.</li><li>Share reproducible methods, results, and limitations.</li></ol><p class="muted">Guided investigations and downloadable example spreadsheets will be added here. No example datasets are represented as real observations yet.</p></div></section></Base>
